## Auth System
### Features
- User registration with hashed password
- JWT authentication with access and refresh tokens

## Roles and Permissions
### Features
- ROLE_ADMIN: Full access to all resources and user management
- ROLE_COLLABORATOR: Access to enterprise management and related resources
- ROLE_WORKER: Access to make macth for a enterprise and related resources
- ROLE_USER: Basic access only views to user-specific resources

## Security
### Features
- Passwords are hashed using bcrypt before storage
- JWT tokens are signed with a secure secret key and have an expiration time
- Refresh tokens are stored securely in the database and can be revoked

## Collaborator and Enterprise Management
### Features
- Collaborators can create and manage enterprise
- Each enterprise has a CNPJ and is associated with a collaborator
- Enterprise can have an address with detailed information (street, number, complement, neighborhood, city)
- Collaborator can and create their job and vacancies view applications
- jobs and vacancies(should has number vacancies) should be created with skills and requirements


#### Endpoints
- POST /auth/register — Create a new user
- POST /auth/login — Authenticate user
- POST /auth/refresh — Refresh JWT access token
- POST /collaborator — Create a new collaborator
- POST /enterprise — Create a new enterprise (collaborator only)
- POST /enterprise/jobs — Create a new job (collaborator only)
- POST /enterprise/vacancies — Create a new vacancy (collaborator only)


